        "problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
        "worked_solution": "Let $u={x}^{2}+1.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,\u27f9\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(2\\sqrt{u})+C \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{u}+C \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
